        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0773" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg651"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loring to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 9, 1889</date>.
                        (Received August 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Lewis’ dispatch 163, dated
                    28th February last, referring to the involuntary infraction by Captain Colcord,
                    of the American bark <hi rendition="#italic">Carrie Heckle</hi>, of a port
                    regulation at Lourenco Marques, and for which he was fined £15 by the
                    custom-house authorities at that port, I have now the honor to inclose copy and
                    translation of note received from the minister of foreign affairs, dated 7th
                    August, instant, stating that the fine exacted from Captain Colcord will be
                    returned to him or his representative.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. B. Loring.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d288-a1.xml" xpointer="d288-a1"/>
